<title>USA: USDA, EGYPT AMBASSADOR MEET ON WHEAT DECREE.</title>
<headline>USDA, EGYPT AMBASSADOR MEET ON WHEAT DECREE.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman and Egypt's ambassador met Thursday to discuss a decree against genetically modified crops that has cast a shadow on U.S. grain exports.</p>
<p>&quot;We indicated we hoped to hear soon a favorable decision on the decree,&quot; Glickmans' trade advisor, Paul Drazek, said afterward.</p>
<p>USDA has argued the decree will impair Egypt's ability to import foodstuffs and that U.S. food crops are safe. For some crops, such as wheat, there is no gentically modified strain.</p>
<p>The United States hopes to see open access to the Egyptian market.</p>
</text>
